00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:03.420
In this short video, I'm going
to demonstrate how you can take a

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:07.950
screen print and insert that into
a document, save that document

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:09.660
and then open it at a later date.

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:13.890
A screen print is basically
a snapshot of whatever is on

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:15.540
the screen at that given time.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:19.890
So if you press the print screen button,
it would take a photograph and then

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:21.600
that would be stored onto the clipboard.

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:25.724
As you work through the course, you'll
be required to provide several screen

00:00:25.724 --> 00:00:30.104
prints in each assessment document to
evidence that you have used a specific

00:00:30.104 --> 00:00:32.144
tool or carried out a specific task.

00:00:33.165 --> 00:00:34.845
So to take a screen print.

00:00:34.905 --> 00:00:38.235
You would need to use the print
screen button, and this will be

00:00:38.235 --> 00:00:40.875
labeled P R T S C on your keyboard.

00:00:41.504 --> 00:00:45.165
If you are using a more modern laptop, you
may find that you have to hold down the

00:00:45.275 --> 00:00:47.955
fn to activate the print screen button.

00:00:50.025 --> 00:00:54.525
So to demonstrate the print screen,
I'm going to open up a folder, which

00:00:54.525 --> 00:00:56.685
contains my Word processing materials.

00:00:57.105 --> 00:01:01.155
And I'm going to take a  snapshot of
that, a print screen of that folder.

00:01:01.605 --> 00:01:04.545
So what I need to do is I'm going
to hold down the alt key and

00:01:04.545 --> 00:01:06.045
press the print screen button.

00:01:06.705 --> 00:01:11.205
Now nothing would appear to have happened,
but a snapshot has been taken and

00:01:11.205 --> 00:01:12.705
that has been stored on the clipboard.

00:01:12.915 --> 00:01:16.875
So if I now go to a Word document and
I'll just open a blank word document.

00:01:17.535 --> 00:01:21.965
And then I can select paste or use
the shortcut key Control and V.

00:01:22.785 --> 00:01:27.435
As you can see, that has then pasted
the snapshot into the Word document.

00:01:30.914 --> 00:01:33.914
So now I have satisfied that
I have the screen print in the

00:01:33.914 --> 00:01:35.384
document, and I'm happy with that.

00:01:35.835 --> 00:01:39.085
I'll go to File and then Save As.

00:01:39.735 --> 00:01:42.465
I want to save  that into
my word processing folder.

00:01:43.335 --> 00:01:44.655
So navigate to the folder.

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:53.640
And then give it the name screenprint
and then save that into that folder.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:58.470
Then if I wanted to open it again
I would just access the folder,

00:01:59.039 --> 00:02:02.370
double click on the screen print,
and that would bring that up.

00:02:03.465 --> 00:02:07.605
As I say, you will be required to complete
several screen prints for each assessment.

00:02:08.385 --> 00:02:11.235
Another thing to bear in mind
is that if you're asked to take

00:02:11.235 --> 00:02:13.635
a screen print to show that
everything that is in the documents.

00:02:13.635 --> 00:02:17.205
So if you have a three-page document,
you will find it beneficial to zoom

00:02:17.205 --> 00:02:24.655
out, which will then allow if you had
more than one page, it will actually

00:02:24.745 --> 00:02:28.265
allow you still to take just the
one screen print to show everything

00:02:28.325 --> 00:02:31.235
that is actually on the three pages.

